<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eteocretans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Eteocretans, 'true Cretans', were descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>'s pre-Greek population who lived in the east of the island in historical times. Their centre was Praisos, and they wrote inscriptions in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-alphabet">Greek alphabet</a> in a still-undeciphered language, Eteocretan, down to the 3rd century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homer">Homer</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odyssey">Odyssey</a> already names them among the island's peoples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/eteocretans.jpg" alt="Eteocretans" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cretophilus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Earliest_Eteocretan_inscription_from_Praisos.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
